  "investigation_history": [
    "The first subscription campaign killed sixteen mutants and left four survivors. Added pre-next invalidation, a valid alternate forbidden native method, and independently valid mismatched grant/filter snapshots; all twenty-seven final variants are killed.",
    "One intermediate native baseline failed without retained diagnostics. It supplies no mutation success. Baseline diagnostics now stay outside the checkout; the complete final serial campaign passed. No product concurrency guarantee is inferred from serial suite scheduling.",
    "An intermediate domain campaign stopped at a stale close-reset mutation site. The point was updated for subscription disposal and the complete twenty-mutant campaign passed.",
    "Installed access first failed because Shell known-folder expansion needed a variable absent from the native minimal environment. The location adapter now uses machine configuration and the OS system drive; four final mutants are killed.",
    "The first installed owner fixture was created under elevation with private owner ACLs. Correctly refused reads were not a product regression. The fixture is now created by the ordinary owner; only access issuance/revocation uses UAC.",
    "The first frontend observation baseline used an invalid empty snapshot fixture. A valid ABSENT item fixed the fixture; all one hundred frontend cases pass.",
    "Two release packaging attempts used the old core because staging was refused by sandbox filesystem access. Neither was installed or counted as fixed-artifact evidence. The final staging used verified same-workspace moves and the installed inventory was checked byte-for-byte."
  ],
